                0.88,
                0.165
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_9_table_2.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>Month, t</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>2</td><td>3</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Height, h (m)</td><td>3</td><td>2.5</td><td>2</td><td>1.5</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.178,
            0.885,
            0.24
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In the example above, as the value of t increases by a fixed number (one month), the value of the height h decreases by a fixed number (0.5). Therefore, this example represents "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "linear decay",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.254,
            0.399,
            0.278
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think and Reflect"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.291,
            0.725,
            0.312
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What will be the height of the water at the end of 5 months?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.327,
            0.886,
            0.406
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Linear growth describes a linear pattern where a quantity increases by a constant amount over equal intervals. Similarly, linear decay describes a linear pattern where a quantity decreases by a constant amount over equal intervals."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.373,
            0.434,
            0.624,
            0.464
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Exercise Set 2.4"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.48,
            0.885,
            0.521
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Suppose a plant has height 1.75 feet and it grows by 0.5 feet each month."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.528,
            0.57,
            0.55
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Find the height after 7 months."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.555,
            0.886,
            0.597
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Make a table of values for t varying from 0 to 10 months and show how the height, h, increases every month."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.603,
            0.886,
            0.646
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Find an expression that relates h and t, and explain why it represents linear growth."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.655,
            0.886,
            0.697
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. A mobile phone is bought for `10,000. Its value decreases by `800 every year."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.702,
            0.678,
            0.724
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Find the value of the phone after 3 years."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.73,
            0.886,
            0.772
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Make a table of values for t varying from 0 to 8 years and show how the value of the phone, v, depreciates with time."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.777,
            0.886,
            0.82
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Find an expression that relates v and t, and explain why it represents linear decay."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.828,
            0.885,
            0.871
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. The initial population of a village is 750. Every year, 50 people move from a nearby city to the village."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.18,
            0.874,
            0.74,
            0.897
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Find the population of the village after 6 years."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
